 <p>In the context menu: "Transcribe message locally with Whisper", "View transcription", "Transcribe again" and "Delete transcription".</p>
 <ul>
   <li><strong>Components:</strong> <em>faster-whisper</em> is the default and comes with WinZapp; <em>whisper.cpp</em> is optional and experimental, and the tab installs it in the version for the processor or for NVIDIA graphics cards. faster-whisper also uses an NVIDIA card once you install the "CUDA libraries" in the same tab.</li>
-  <li><strong>Models:</strong> they are only downloaded when you ask, from tiny to large-v3 and large-v3-turbo; in whisper.cpp there are also smaller versions (8 and 5 bits) and some 32-bit ones. Some models understand only one language (marked in the list). In the list, Ctrl+Space marks models and "Download" downloads all the marked ones, one after the other. "Where to run the transcription" and the "Calculation precision" stay on Automatic or can be chosen.</li>
+  <li><strong>Models:</strong> they are only downloaded when you ask, from tiny to large-v3 and large-v3-turbo; in whisper.cpp there are also smaller versions (8 and 5 bits) and some 32-bit ones. Some models understand only one language (marked in the list). In the list, Ctrl+Space marks models and "Download" downloads all the marked ones, one after the other. "Where to run the transcription" and the "Calculation precision: {precision}" stay on Automatic or can be chosen.</li>
   <li><strong>Reuse what you already have:</strong> "Models in other folders" uses models downloaded elsewhere without copying them, and "Reuse downloads from another folder" points to the CUDA libraries and to the whisper.cpp programs already downloaded. The models folder can be moved, with the models along.</li>
   <li><strong>Memory:</strong> "Keep the model loaded in memory (faster-whisper and whisper.cpp)" avoids reloading the model for each message. Turned off, the model is released 5 minutes after the last transcription.</li>
   <li><strong>Per model:</strong> the text stored in each message is per model. When you switch models, the message is transcribed again and the previous model's text stays stored. "Clear this model's saved transcriptions" and "Clear saved transcriptions of all models" clean the cache. The cache can be turned on or off in general and per model.</li>
   <li><strong>No progress window:</strong> the option "Transcribe without the progress window: stay on the messages or statuses until the text is ready (the same shortcut cancels)" makes Alt+Shift+T and Alt+Shift+N transcribe in the background; the same shortcut on the same message cancels.</li>
   <li><strong>Automatic:</strong> "Automatically transcribe received voice messages and videos and put the text in the message line" transcribes each new voice message and video (up to 10 minutes of audio, one at a time, outside locked chats), with no windows or per-message announcements. If transcription is not ready, WinZapp pauses and says why just once.</li>
-  <li><strong>Enter and Space:</strong> with "Enter and Space on a voice message or video transcribe it into its line in the list instead of playing it..." (Settings &gt; Audio), Enter and Space transcribe and Alt+Shift+N plays or pauses. Turned off, Enter and Space play and Alt+Shift+N transcribes on the row.</li>
+  <li><strong>Enter and Space:</strong> with "Enter and Space on a voice message or video transcribe it into its line in the list instead of playing it" (Settings &gt; Audio), Enter and Space transcribe and Alt+Shift+N plays or pauses. Turned off, Enter and Space play and Alt+Shift+N transcribes on the row.</li>
   <li><strong>Videos:</strong> the video's sound is converted and transcribed, with the same options. GIFs are ignored and a video without sound is reported as such.</li>
   <li><strong>In bulk:</strong> WinZapp says how many messages will be transcribed, skipped or reused, transcribes one at a time ("message 3 of 12"), continues if one fails and says at the end how many succeeded, were skipped and failed. The same shortcut or the context menu cancels the queue, and the context menu shows all the transcriptions together, with sender, date and time, to copy or save. With "Replace shortcuts with bulk actions when selecting chats and messages", Alt+Shift+T and Alt+Shift+N also act on the selection.</li>
   <li><strong>Background downloads:</strong> with "Download updates and transcription downloads in the background, without the progress window" (Settings &gt; General), models, whisper.cpp and CUDA download without the progress window, and "Cancel download in the background" stops it.</li>
@@ -36,9 +36,11 @@
   <tr><td>Photo or video: "Describe"</td><td>Describes the image. A video is described from a single image taken from it; the sound is never sent.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>Sticker: "Describe sticker"</td><td>Describes the sticker.</td></tr>
   <tr><td>PDF: "Convert to accessible text"</td><td>Turns it into plain, readable text.</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Chat with unread messages: "Summarize unread messages"</td><td>Summarizes the open chat's unread messages.</td></tr>
 </table>
 <p><kbd>Ctrl+Shift+I</kbd> does all of this on the focused message. The result opens in a window with the text; for photos and videos, you can ask follow-up questions (Ctrl+Enter asks). In the Status tab (Alt+5), the "Describe" button describes photo and video statuses.</p>
